d-exposed-a-devastating-decline/articleshow/133709507.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-02T17:32:35+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133709780,imgsize-1820983.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Fisherman built this boat in 1929 while raising 13 children; $1.5M is being raised to restore it]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133705664.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A wooden fishing boat built in 1929 is nearing restoration on Martha’s Vineyard, almost a century after it was built beside the home of a family raising 13 children. Little Lady, the sole remaining wooden fishing dragger in New England, is set to undergo major repairs. The $1.5 million project still needs $630,000, while supporters hope to preserve the boat’s history and connection to the island’s fishing community.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1929-a-fisherman-built-a-wooden-boat-beside-the-home-where-he-was-raising-13-children-nearly-a-century-later-1-5-million-is-being-raised-to-restore-it/articleshow/133705664.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1929-a-fisherman-built-a-wooden-boat-beside-the-home-where-he-was-raising-13-children-nearly-a-century-later-1-5-million-is-being-raised-to-restore-it/articleshow/133705664.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-02T18:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133706401,imgsize-151141.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[NY couple spend $3M on a home for their dog; now sell for $2.9M]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133708647.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Howard and Suze Rubin moved their home to New York for their dog. They spent nearly three million dollars renovating the house for Buster's needs. The property features a custom pool and shaded outdoor areas for the dog. This unique home, designed for canine comfort, is now on the market. The couple seeks to return to Florida after enjoying their time in New York.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/in-2019-a-new-york-couple-bought-a-1-825m-ridge-home-for-their-bearded-collie-after-spending-another-2m-on-renovations-busters-retreat-is-now-listed-for-2-9m/articleshow/133708647.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/in-2019-a-new-york-couple-bought-a-1-825m-ridge-home-for-their-bearded-collie-after-spending-another-2m-on-renovations-busters-retreat-is-now-listed-for-2-9m/articleshow/133708647.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-02T17:14:36+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Real Estate Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133709243,imgsize-682681.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Quote of the day by William Shakespeare: "All the world's a stage, and all the men..."]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133709283.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/quote-of-the-day-by-william-shakespeare-all-the-worlds-a-stage-and-all-the-men-and-women-merely-a-timeless-lesson-on-change-identity-and-life/articleshow/133709283.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/quote-of-the-day-by-william-shakespeare-all-the-worlds-a-stage-and-all-the-men-and-women-merely-a-timeless-lesson-on-change-identity-and-life/articleshow/133709283.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-02T17:12:33+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133709390,imgsize-121134.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Woman arrested after allegedly filming jurors in Lindsay Clancy triple-murder trial]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133710183.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/woman-arrested-after-allegedly-filming-jurors-in-lindsay-clancy-triple-murder-trial/articleshow/133710183.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/woman-arrested-after-allegedly-filming-jurors-in-lindsay-clancy-triple-murder-trial/articleshow/133710183.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-02T17:45:18+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133710183,imgsize-78944.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Scientists released 45,000 cfs from Glen Canyon Dam for 8 days in 1996 to rebuild Grand Canyon sandbars]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133708366.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In 1996, a controlled flood was executed in the Grand Canyon to rejuvenate its natural river dynamics. Leveraging the Glen Canyon Dam, scientists released substantial volumes of water to transport sediment downstream, with the goal of restoring sandbars that had diminished due to the dam's existence. This initiative highlighted the potential of dam operations to contribute positively to ecological restoration, paving the way for future river management experiments.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-released-up-to-45000-cubic-feet-of-water-per-second-from-glen-canyon-dam-for-8-days-in-1996-the-artificial-flood-rebuilt-grand-canyon-sandbars/articleshow/133708366.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-released-up-to-45000-cubic-feet-of-water-per-second-from-glen-canyon-dam-for-8-days-in-1996-the-artificial-flood-rebuilt-grand-canyon-sandbars/articleshow/133708366.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-02T17:03:19+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133708621,imgsize-1979667.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[US detonated nuclear bomb to unlock gas; 213M cubic feet were produced, but the gas was radioactive]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133705011.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In 1967, the US detonated a 29-kiloton nuclear device 4,227 feet underground in New Mexico to boost natural gas production. Five tests produced 213 million cubic feet of gas, but it contained measurable radioactivity. The experiment was later ended, the site cleaned up, and radioactive contamination remains underground in the blast zone.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-1967-the-us-detonated-a-29-kiloton-nuclear-device-4227-feet-below-new-mexico-to-unlock-natural-gas-5-tests-produced-213-million-cubic-feet-but-the-gas-had-measurable-radioactivity/articleshow/133705011.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-1967-the-us-detonated-a-29-kiloton-nuclear-device-4227-feet-below-new-mexico-to-unlock-natural-gas-5-tests-produced-213-million-cubic-feet-but-the-gas-had-measurable-radioactivity/articleshow/133705011.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-02T17:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133705414,imgsize-162913.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Robert Stack owned California acreage with a private game preserve in the 1970s]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133708419.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-the-1970s-actor-robert-stack-owned-california-acreage-that-included-a-private-game-preserve-his-unusual-landholding-offered-a-glimpse-into-hollywoods-forgotten-ranch-culture/articleshow/133708419.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-the-1970s-actor-robert-stack-owned-california-acreage-that-included-a-private-game-preserve-his-unusual-landholding-offered-a-glimpse-into-hollywoods-forgotten-ranch-culture/articleshow/133708419.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-02T16:58:49+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133708831,imgsize-2554196.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Glacier collapse at 8.37am, alert at 9.15: Why Nepal sent disaster warning 38 mins late]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133707274.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/south-asia/glacier-collapse-at-8-37am-alert-at-9-15-why-nepal-sent-disaster-warning-38-minutes-late/articleshow/133707274.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/south-asia/glacier-collapse-at-8-37am-alert-at-9-15-why-nepal-sent-disaster-warning-38-minutes-late/articleshow/133707274.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-02T16:32:14+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aastha Jha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133708039,imgsize-255408.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['November is a priority’: Trump aides push to contain Iran war until midterm elections]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133706799.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Top Trump aides push to prevent Iran war escalation before November elections. The administration is focusing on economic pressure to secure concessions from Iran. Recent exchanges of strikes have increased tensions between the US and Iran. Military readiness and depleted munitions stockpiles also constrain White House strategy. America's Gulf allies are urging the White House to de-escalate the conflict.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/november-is-a-priority-donald-trump-aides-push-to-contain-iran-war-until-midterm-elections/articleshow/133706799.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/november-is-a-priority-donald-trump-aides-push-to-contain-iran-war-until-midterm-elections/articleshow/133706799.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-02T16:07:47+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133707203,imgsize-890315.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[On this day in 1666: The Great Fire of London sparked a housing crisis, leaving 100,000 homeless]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133705761.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/on-this-day-in-1666-the-great-fire-of-london-sparked-a-housing-crisis-leaving-100000-homeless/articleshow/133705761.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatim