5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133705432.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[More than 6,100 Ebola cases and 3,000 deaths are recorded in the Democratic Republic of Congo.  Weak surveillance and insecurity hinder efforts to contain the nation's worst-ever epidemic.  Schools have reopened amid concerns about potential transmission within classrooms.  No approved vaccine exists for the Bundibugyo species, though some are in development.  Britain has pledged over fifty million pounds to support outbreak containment efforts.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/congos-ebola-death-toll-crosses-3000-amid-worst-outbreak-in-countrys-history-cases-top-6100/articleshow/133705432.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/congos-ebola-death-toll-crosses-3000-amid-worst-outbreak-in-countrys-history-cases-top-6100/articleshow/133705432.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-02T15:07:18+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133705674,imgsize-175560.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[After 286 days at sea, USS Abraham Lincoln arrives in Thailand; authorities raid sex workers]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133705354.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/after-286-days-at-sea-uss-abraham-lincoln-arrives-in-thailand-authorities-raid-sex-workers/articleshow/133705354.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/after-286-days-at-sea-uss-abraham-lincoln-arrives-in-thailand-authorities-raid-sex-workers/articleshow/133705354.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-02T15:02:12+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aastha Jha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133705579,imgsize-71198.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[New Zealand’s heaviest parrot surges from 51 to 325 after decades of conservation]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133704829.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/new-zealands-worlds-heaviest-parrot-was-on-the-brink-with-only-51-birds-left-now-after-decades-of-intensive-conservation-by-wildlife-experts-its-population-has-surged-to-325/articleshow/133704829.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/new-zealands-worlds-heaviest-parrot-was-on-the-brink-with-only-51-birds-left-now-after-decades-of-intensive-conservation-by-wildlife-experts-its-population-has-surged-to-325/articleshow/133704829.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-02T14:31:18+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133704973,imgsize-1448280.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[12 artificial reefs created in 1998 boosted local fish numbers and species richness off Miami Beach]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133700538.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A 2002 study examined 12 artificial reefs built off Miami Beach using limestone boulders, concrete-gravel aggregate and concrete mixed with waste tyre chips. Divers surveyed the reefs every two months from October 1998 to February 2001, recording fish species, numbers and sizes, along with spiny lobsters. They counted 97,826 fish from 146 species. The researchers found no significant difference in fish abundance, biomass or species richness between the three reef materials. However, comparisons before and after deployment showed that the artificial reefs increased local fish abundance and species richness.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-1998-researchers-built-12-reefs-off-miami-beach-using-limestone-concrete-and-concrete-mixed-with-waste-tyre-chips-divers-later-counted-97826-fish-from-146-species/articleshow/133700538.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-1998-researchers-built-12-reefs-off-miami-beach-using-limestone-concrete-and-concrete-mixed-with-waste-tyre-chips-divers-later-counted-97826-fish-from-146-species/articleshow/133700538.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-02T14:29:10+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133701795,imgsize-99829.cms"/></item></channel></rss>